em as stated like  do we even have the data and so this is  like early phase work maybe we have the  data do we know how to build the  algorithm like does it actually work on  our systems and the answer to this could  be no and then you might go back to you  CTO and say sorry we don't we need to  react cheer Accord the data we don't  have anything but suppose that we  actually do so you might engage your  data scientists and data engineers at  this point and if that passes we'll go  on to the next step what does a Minimum  Viable Product look like and this at  this point you should be engaging thing  people like your designers and your  product managers so that they can manage  the process of your work as you move  forward and you may even fail at this  because you may not come up with a good  solution of what a product  I mean Viable Product looks like and  that would tell you that like you could  do all the best machine learning in the  world but you're not going to get to a  place where it's going to work because  it doesn't fit in with the rest of your  product vision assuming you can do that  the next question is how do we build the  MVP and at this point you need to be  engaging other people you need to be  engaging your back-end team your  front-end team your infrastructure team  and figuring out how things work and  then if that works then you move on how  do we ship the MVP and you bring in even  more people and this is where you have  compliance legal QA all of that stuff  and what we're doing here is we're  engaging people early in the process so  that we don't get to the points where  we're having difficulties with like oh  we've deployed a machine learning  algorithm why is it now all of a sudden  banning all these people from our  platform that we didn't want to ban and  creating a huge public relations  nightmare for us not that I'm looking at  any social media platforms when I think  of this example and then finally how do  we improve the MVP so we'v